From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:08:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: Take G16's RTKit from the bound-device
 registration

Firn's RTKit abstraction has the handler borrow nothing and get its
callbacks through &self, with buffers mapped by Operations::shmem_map().
Make BootData the handler and keep the registration in Bootstrap through
Registration::new_devres(), which the GPU device owns until it unbinds.
Runtime messages go through send_message(), which fails once the device
is gone. The platform driver's unbind() marks the DRM device failed, so
clients that keep it open see errors, and puts the firmware to sleep
while the device is still bound; if that fails, the GPU mappings are
kept. CrashBuffer now hands RTKit a byte slice of the reserved region.

Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
